Z||000012||fierodave||06-12-2000||11:45 AM||||UPDATE   pulled the plugs connecting the ECM and cleaned the contacts!  NO go!<BR>when I did this I noticed it had junk yard lettering on the ECM & the nuts that hold the ECM tight were gone  hmmmmm<BR>I replaced the ECM and switched the prom chip and it runs like a dream!!<BR>has the three stag idle down as it was designed to do!<BR>it was worked on prior to my purchase<BR>they said it ran like that for years<BR>they took it to three different placed and no one could figure it out!  Damn  I'm an idiot when it comes to computers, but could see there was a problem!  maybe that's why I got the car for $500 instead of the $1,600.00 asking price?  ;~)<BR>thanks for all the help on this one guys!  I am not afraid to do a ECM now!!<BR>thanks for the space<BR>FD||||reg||1
Z||000013||LarryB||06-12-2000||01:07 PM||||Dave, for future reference to check the IAC warm up the engine, shut it off, then pull the 2-wire connector off the IAC.  When you start the car it should immediately go to about 3000 RPM or so. Easier than removing and replacing it. <P>Just be sure the ignition is off when you unplug the IAC connector and again when you go to plug the connector back in. When you plug it back in the next time you start it should idle 'normally'.<p>[This message has been edited by LarryB (edited 06-12-2000).]||||reg||1
